 the  mother box in general there's a lot of  aspects that don't make sense in this  scene  firstly while transporting the box out  of the building  the queen stops and has a dramatic  moment to talk to one of her fallen  comrades  like why the hell is she talking to this  girl she's literally surrounded by  parademons and is in immediate danger  she should be getting the hell out of  there because their sole objective is to  get the mother box away from steppenwolf  but i guess talking to a dying amazonian  is more important  after that they then seal the chamber  but what's the point in sealing it when  there's a massive hole in the ceiling  that they can just fly out of  if anything the amazonians are just  killing more of their own here  i also don't assume they survived  because for whatever reason  sealing the chamber somehow makes the  cliff self-destruct and fall into the  ocean  which in of itself i don't know how they  made that happen  then instead of getting the hell out of  there the queen decides to just stare at  the wreckage  like everyone should know steppenwolf is  fine he's literally flexing arrows out  of his armor and he's getting dog piled  by beefy woman  so some rubble should be nothing for him  and while staring at the wreckage  surprise surprise he emerges  great job he could have been running for  the hills by now  so for this scene i want to add a  suggestion to make it less devoid of  logic  i think it would have been much better  to have a darth vader style holloway  fight scene  of steppenwolf demolishing his way  through all the amazonians to get to the  mother box  action-wise it would be much more badass  and it would solve the whole ceiling  access issue  having a build up of him fighting  through the hallway would make the  progression of this action scene  much better and then when he gets there  they can try to extract the motherbox  so moving on we have another aquaman  scene  i like how he keeps throwing away his  shirts before he goes back into the  water  like where does he get all these shirts  from this just reminds me of the whole  hulk conundrum where he always has a new  pair of clothes after he hulks out  during the whole flashback sequence  where darkseid is trying to dominate  earth  he is for some reason not doing it with  any armor  as a result of that he just gets one  tapped by an axe and runs home  crying that is both stupid on darkseid's  part and on the filmmaker's standpoint  because how are we supposed to treat  darkseid as a menacing and intimidating  villain  when he immediately gets rolled i don't  know if he underestimated earth or  something  but not wearing armor in general is a  bad idea  you don't see thanos walking around  shirtless although i would assume some  fans may want to see that  also i like how one roman is giving  batman this whole 10 minute exposition  monologue  i'm just surprised he hasn't fallen  asleep yet so  moving on to the next scene we have  steppenwolf and tara getting people for  information  as to where the atlantean mother box is  for this moment i just wanted to point  out a macguffin device that steppenwolf  has that allows him to read people's  minds  like wow that's oddly convenient for the  plot  why does steppenwolf even ask this guy  where their mother box is  when he can just read his mind where is  it  no son of daughter of atlantis will ever  tell  in the scene where batman meets flash he  first says this  i know you have abilities i just don't  know what they are  and then he proceeds to throw a batarang  right at his face  if you were uncertain as to whether or  not he could actually see things in  bullet time  then why would you throw a batarang at  him that could have instantly killed him  i wonder if batman did this before and  showed up to the wrong person's  apartment and just headshotted them  so going back to the mother boxes and  the anti-life equation  there is a scene where steppenwolf has a  vision that the anti-